  "rust_summary": "F4M-10: the hooks a WASM guest implements to script fully custom mobs (goals, lifecycle, interaction, pose).",
  "doc_summary": "F4M-10 script hooks of fully custom mobs (`native_mob_goal_can_use`, `native_mob_tick`, `native_mob_hurt`, `native_mob_pose` and the rest). The game reaches the WASM guest of a server module through the `mobs::custom::script::Runtime` it installs, not through these functions: they exist so the catalog (and the generated WIT, SDK and adapters) has one place that names every export and its types. Bundles need hooks version @API:mob_goal_can_use@.",
